<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balkars</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Balkars are a Turkic-speaking people of the high valleys of the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a>, living mainly in Kabardino-Balkaria in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, and their language is close to that of the Karachays. Long dependent on the Kabardian princes, they came under Russian rule in the 19th century. In 1944 Stalin deported the whole people to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, and they were allowed to return only in 1957.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/balkars.jpg" alt="Balkars" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mór Déchy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balkar_Elders.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
